    git clone <repository_url>
    cd <project_directory>
    ```

2.  **Install dependencies:**

    ```bash
    npm install  # or yarn install
    ```

3.  **Start the development server:**

    ```bash
    npm start  # or yarn start
    ```

    This will start the application in development mode. Open your browser and navigate to `http://localhost:3000` to view it.

## Usage Examples

### Adding a New Project

1.  Navigate to the `src/components/Projects` directory.
2.  Create a new component file for your project (e.g., `MyNewProject.js`).
3.  Import the new component into the `Projects.js` file.
4.  Add the new project to the projects array in `Projects.js`.

```javascript
// src/components/Projects/MyNewProject.js
import React from 'react';

const MyNewProject = () => {
  return (
    <div className="project">
      <h3>My New Project</h3>
      <p>Description of my new project.</p>
      <a href="https://github.com/your-username/my-new-project">GitHub Repository</a>
    </div>
  );
};

export default MyNewProject;

// src/components/Projects/Projects.js
import React from 'react';
import MyNewProject from './MyNewProject';

const Projects = () => {
  const projects = [
    // ... existing projects
    {
      id: 'my-new-project',
      component: <MyNewProject />,
    },
  ];

  return (
    <div className="projects">
      {projects.map((project) => (
        <div key={project.id}>{project.component}</div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Projects;
```

### Updating the About Me Section

1.  Open the `src/components/About.js` file.
2.  Edit the content within the component to reflect your personal information, skills, and experience.

```javascript
// src/components/About.js
import React from 'react';

const About = () => {
  return (
    <div className="about">
      <h2>About Me</h2>
      <p>
        I am a software engineer with a passion for building innovative and user-friendly applications.
        I have experience in React, Node.js, and other modern technologies.
      </p>
    </div>
  );
};

export default About;
```

